      "content": "Elias's peace isn't a bright dawn but a quiet surrender to the gray, where he finally stops fighting the weight of his own failure. He finds rest not in hope, but in the acceptance that his pain is the only truth left, and he chooses to let it be. This ending feels real because it honors his exhaustion, showing that sometimes the only way to stop hurting is to stop trying to fix it.",
